# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Collectee — environment
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill it in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is
# not, so never put a real key here.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Restart the dev server after editing — Expo reads env at bundle time, so a
# running server will not pick up a change.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── AI (PRD §12.1's "one real model call") ───────────────────────────────────
# There is exactly ONE AI setting in this app, and it is a URL. The client reads
# no key on any code path — see the warning at the bottom of this file.
#
# SET THIS TO THE DEPLOYED PROXY. It is live — paste the line below verbatim:
#
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_AI_PROXY_URL=https://collectee.vercel.app/api/assistant
#
# ⚠️ Use that STABLE ALIAS, not the per-deployment URL `vercel deploy` prints.
# Every production deploy mints a new immutable hostname
# (collectee-56mzka9n0-collectee.vercel.app and so on); the alias always tracks
# current production, so it survives the next redeploy and the one after that.
#
# ONE endpoint serves all three capabilities — article summaries, the per-game
# trends digest, and the in-app assistant's chat — so this is the only URL to
# configure, and one deploy lights up all three.
#
# Leave BLANK and everything still works: the article screen keeps its prepared
# summaries, the news screen its prepared digests, and the assistant answers
# from on-device data. All three say so on screen rather than implying a model
# ran. Both feature flags now ship TRUE (src/config/features.ts), so a blank URL
# here is the only thing standing between you and the live path.
#
# ⚠️ A blank URL and a broken URL look IDENTICAL on screen — both show the
# prepared copy, by design. If you expect live output and are not getting it,
# check this value before you go looking for a bug.
EXPO_PUBLIC_AI_PROXY_URL=

# ⚠️ THE ANTHROPIC KEY DOES NOT GO IN THIS FILE.
#
# It is billed, and every EXPO_PUBLIC_* value is bundled into the shipped
# JavaScript where anyone with the app can read it. The key belongs in Vercel's
# environment variables for the deployed function, under the name
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY — set via the project's Settings → Environment Variables
# page. It is never read by the app.
#
# It is already set on the `collectee` project, so you do not need it to run
# this build. Nobody needs a copy of the key to develop against the live proxy;
# they need the URL above and nothing else.
#
# Prefer the dashboard over `vercel env add`: run through a non-interactive
# shell that command demands `--value "<the key>"` on the command line, which
# puts the key in shell history and in any session transcript.
